OL,3,GNEWSABlood cancer patients call for
OL,4,Afaster drug access
OL,5,
OL,6,FPatients with incurable blood cancer
OL,7,Fsay they fear they will die if new
OL,8,Ftreatments are not made available more
OL,9,Fquickly.
OL,11,FLouise Martinez from Berkshire has been
OL,12,Fliving with myeloma for 5 years. She
OL,13,Fhas joined a national campaign calling
OL,14,Ffor more drugs to be made available.
OL,16,FThe 50-year-old has been on four rounds
OL,17,Fof treatment and is worried that the
OL,18,Fbest new drugs won't be available for
OL,19,Fher when she needs them. The condition
OL,20,Fcan damage bones, weaken the immune
OL,21,Fsystem and harm organs.
OL,23,APub: 23-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
